{"type":"message","id":"d7da0f84","parentId":"295e1f27","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:00:50.300Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_RpynioeOEs1pKPfQPjvkjlQq","toolName":"process","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-carolina-governor-signs-bill-protecting-bitcoin-miners-banning-cbdc\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"South Carolina has passed S. Bill 163, banning state agencies from accepting CBDCs, protecting crypto self-custody rights, and exempting Bitcoin miners from money transmitter licensing requirements.\"\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"South Carolina Governor Signs Bill Protecting Bitcoin Miners and Banning CBDC Payments\"\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"South Carolina has passed S. Bill 163, banning state agencies from accepting CBDCs, protecting crypto self-custody rights, and exempting Bitcoin miners from money transmitter licensing requirements.\"\n---\n### https://decrypt.co/368455/south-carolina-law-banning-cbdc-protecting-crypto-users-bitcoin-miners\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"The crypto-friendly legislation was signed into law on Tuesday, granting protections to crypto users, developers, and Bitcoin miners.\"\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"South Carolina Passes Law Banning CBDCs While Protecting Crypto Users, Bitcoin Miners - Decrypt\"\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"The crypto-friendly legislation was signed into law on Tuesday, granting protections to crypto users, developers, and Bitcoin miners.\"\n---\n\n\nProcess exited with code 0."}],"details":{"status":"completed","sessionId":"tender-falcon","exitCode":0,"aggregated":"### https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-carolina-governor-signs-bill-protecting-bitcoin-miners-banning-cbdc\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"South Carolina has passed S. Bill 163, banning state agencies from accepting CBDCs, protecting crypto self-custody rights, and exempting Bitcoin miners from money transmitter licensing requirements.\"\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"South Carolina Governor Signs Bill Protecting Bitcoin Miners and Banning CBDC Payments\"\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"South Carolina has passed S. Bill 163, banning state agencies from accepting CBDCs, protecting crypto self-custody rights, and exempting Bitcoin miners from money transmitter licensing requirements.\"\n---\n### https://decrypt.co/368455/south-carolina-law-banning-cbdc-protecting-crypto-users-bitcoin-miners\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"The crypto-friendly legislation was signed into law on Tuesday, granting protections to crypto users, developers, and Bitcoin miners.\"\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"South Carolina Passes Law Banning CBDCs While Protecting Crypto Users, Bitcoin Miners - Decrypt\"\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"The crypto-friendly legislation was signed into law on Tuesday, granting protections to crypto users, developers, and Bitcoin miners.\"\n---\n","name":"set pipefail"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779343250300}}
{"type":"message","id":"33d55ae0","parentId":"d7da0f84","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:00:57.549Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_vYv1tnHRQOIBgilZqqH85dvA","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -L -s --max-time 20 'https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-carolina-governor-signs-bill-protecting-bitcoin-miners-banning-cbdc' | grep -oP '<p[^>]*>[^<]{20,}</p>' | sed -n '1,40p'","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher","yieldMs":5000,"timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":694,"output":704,"cacheRead":23168,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24566,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779343250302,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhqkcJyORh7RvRF56aHzJS1fzgaMr"}}
{"type":"message","id":"59ffdd29","parentId":"33d55ae0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:00:57.869Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_vYv1tnHRQOIBgilZqqH85dvA","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<p class=\"my-3 text-base/normal tracking-tight text-pretty text-ct-ds-fg-default tablet:mt-5 tablet:mb-4 tablet:text-lg/normal\" data-testid=\"post__description\">Senate Bill 163 bans CBDC payments by state agencies and shields Bitcoin miners from discriminatory zoning and licensing rules.</p>\n<p>South Carolina Governor Henry McMaster signed Senate Bill 163 into law on Tuesday, advancing one of the most crypto-friendly state-level frameworks in the country.</p>\n<p>On CBDCs, the law bars any state agency or political subdivision from accepting, requiring payment in, or participating in Federal Reserve-led digital currency trials, including any pilot programs run by federal agencies.</p>\n<p>It also protects crypto self-custody rights, preventing governments from restricting the use of hardware and self-hosted wallets while barring higher taxes on crypto transactions than comparable payments made in US dollars.</p>\n<p>The bill gives Bitcoin miners operating in industrial zones specific protections. Local governments cannot impose restrictions on mining businesses that do not apply to other industrial operations in the same area, and cannot set mining-specific noise limits beyond what general pollution rules already require.</p>\n<p>“A political subdivision shall not change the zoning of a digital asset mining business without going through the proper notice and comment. A digital asset mining business may appeal a change in zoning to the proper court of jurisdiction,” the bill reads.</p>\n<p>The law also exempts several activities from money transmitter licensing requirements, including mining, node operation, blockchain software development and crypto-to-crypto trading. Mining-as-a-service and staking-as-a-service providers are excluded from securities classification.</p>\n<p>Oklahoma, Arkansas, Florida, Mississippi, Montana, North Dakota, Louisiana and Arizona are among the states that have passed similar pieces of crypto legislation in recent years.</p>\n<p> Cointelegraph is committed to providing independent, high-quality journalism across the crypto, blockchain, AI, and fintech industries. </p>"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":307,"aggregated":"<p class=\"my-3 text-base/normal tracking-tight text-pretty text-ct-ds-fg-default tablet:mt-5 tablet:mb-4 tablet:text-lg/normal\" data-testid=\"post__description\">Senate Bill 163 bans CBDC payments by state agencies and shields Bitcoin miners from discriminatory zoning and licensing rules.</p>\n<p>South Carolina Governor Henry McMaster signed Senate Bill 163 into law on Tuesday, advancing one of the most crypto-friendly state-level frameworks in the country.</p>\n<p>On CBDCs, the law bars any state agency or political subdivision from accepting, requiring payment in, or participating in Federal Reserve-led digital currency trials, including any pilot programs run by federal agencies.</p>\n<p>It also protects crypto self-custody rights, preventing governments from restricting the use of hardware and self-hosted wallets while barring higher taxes on crypto transactions than comparable payments made in US dollars.</p>\n<p>The bill gives Bitcoin miners operating in industrial zones specific protections. Local governments cannot impose restrictions on mining businesses that do not apply to other industrial operations in the same area, and cannot set mining-specific noise limits beyond what general pollution rules already require.</p>\n<p>“A political subdivision shall not change the zoning of a digital asset mining business without going through the proper notice and comment. A digital asset mining business may appeal a change in zoning to the proper court of jurisdiction,” the bill reads.</p>\n<p>The law also exempts several activities from money transmitter licensing requirements, including mining, node operation, blockchain software development and crypto-to-crypto trading. Mining-as-a-service and staking-as-a-service providers are excluded from securities classification.</p>\n<p>Oklahoma, Arkansas, Florida, Mississippi, Montana, North Dakota, Louisiana and Arizona are among the states that have passed similar pieces of crypto legislation in recent years.</p>\n<p> Cointelegraph is committed to providing independent, high-quality journalism across the crypto, blockchain, AI, and fintech industries. </p>","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779343257869}}
